The Go game server (tools/d1/cmd/d1-srv, built to d1-server/target/release/d1-srv) runs only
under d1-nonet: it owns the accounts and starts d1-recomp as its child inside the same applied
game profile. Listing it with the game binaries makes the hook admit
`d1-nonet <root>/d1-server/target/release/d1-srv ...` for agent test runs, and makes d1-localonly
and the hook refuse it anywhere else. d1-srv carries no C gate (it is Go, no cgo); it checks its
own containment at start with the gate's loopback probe and exits 2 if not refused.

Owner applies: git apply containment/proposals/2026-10-18-d1-srv.patch, then reinstall the hook.

--- a/containment/go/gate/local.go
+++ b/containment/go/gate/local.go
@@ -47,5 +47,6 @@
 }

-// GameBinaries run game code and carry the C gate, so they run only under d1-nonet.
-var GameBinaries = []string{"d1-recomp", "d1-oracle", "d1-replay"}
+// GameBinaries run game code (or, d1-srv, start it) and run only under d1-nonet. The Rust three
+// carry the C gate; d1-srv probes its own containment at start.
+var GameBinaries = []string{"d1-recomp", "d1-oracle", "d1-replay", "d1-srv"}

